<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Motion categories following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hanyu et al. (2023)</a></cite>, with human performance, counts, and visual examples.
Human F1 scores are reported as forward (F)/backward (B) for each motion category.
AoT-PsyPhyBENCH  includes categories 1–5 (all clips) and excludes category 6.
<span id="S4.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#009900;">✓</span> marks categories where reversal is typically easy for humans (irreversible processes); <span id="S4.T1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#B30000;">✗</span> marks cyclic, bidirectional motions where reversal is challenging.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
